Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimePedestrianCrossingAnomaly" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Pedestrian walking into the roadway from the side, not using a crosswalk" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Pedestrian entering vehicle path without warning" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Limited visibility due to nighttime and pedestrian emerging from poorly lit area" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.92"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.88"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Pedestrian entering vehicle path without warning
Severity Score: 0.92

**Risk 2:**
Description: Limited visibility due to nighttime and pedestrian emerging from poorly lit area
Severity Score: 0.88